Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [Model][Engram] Name disk shards by vocab slice, not rank
 alone

A rank hosts one shard per Engram layer, so the rank alone does not name a
shard. DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash has two Engram layers (ids 1 and 14), and both
mapped <dir>/engram_r<rank>: the second layer to load clobbered the first,
leaving four files where there should be eight and serving both layers from
one table. A benchmark cannot see this -- random prompts with --ignore-eos
never check output -- and the unit tests missed it because they build a
single embedding.

Key the path on this shard's vocab slice as well, which is what actually
distinguishes the two layers' tables on a rank.

