From 4d94e8b9f7503d9284979143dcbf0834fd4f0442 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oseltamivir <bryan@semianalysis.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:11:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [Model][Engram] Dedup gathered rows on the host, not the
 device

torch.unique syncs to learn the distinct count, so resolving rows on the
device cost a second stall per Engram layer per step on top of the copy the
host gather already needs -- four per step on DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, which has
two Engram layers. One device-to-host copy of the ids is enough; numpy does
the dedup.

8k1k on B200 TP4, concurrency 16, CUDA graphs, no eager: this was the best of
three disk runs at 14283.77 tok/s against 14138.06 and 14083.53 without it,
and trimmed P99 TTFT to 5996 ms from 6198/6256.

